Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: User Cannot See Expected Resources
Problem: User logs in but cannot see projects, inventories, or job templates they should have access to.

Solution:

Verify the user is assigned to the correct team
Check that the team has the appropriate role on the resource
Ensure the resource belongs to the same organization as the user
Refresh the browser or clear cache
Issue 2: Permission Denied When Executing Job Templates
Problem: User can see job template but gets permission denied when trying to execute.

Solution:

Verify the user/team has Execute role on the job template
Check that the user has Use role on the associated project
Ensure the user has appropriate access to the inventory
Verify all credential requirements are met
Issue 3: Team Members Not Inheriting Team Permissions
Problem: Users added to teams don't automatically get team permissions.

Solution:

Confirm the user is properly added to the team
Verify team permissions are correctly configured
Check organization membership alignment
Have the user log out and log back in
Issue 4: Unable to Assign Roles
Problem: Cannot assign roles to users or teams.

Solution:

Ensure you have admin privileges on the resource
Verify the target user/team exists and is active
Check organization boundaries - users can only be granted roles within their organization
Confirm the role type is appropriate for the resource
Verification and Testing Commands
To verify your configuration from the command line (if needed), you can use these AWX CLI commands:

# Install AWX CLI (if not already installed)
pip3 install awxkit

# Configure AWX CLI
export CONTROLLER_HOST=https://your-awx-host
export CONTROLLER_USERNAME=admin
export CONTROLLER_PASSWORD=admin123

# List all users
awx users list

# List all teams
awx teams list

# Show user roles
awx users get <user_id> --related roles

# Show team roles
awx teams get <team_id> --related roles
Security Best Practices Implemented
Throughout this lab, we've implemented several security best practices:

Principle of Least Privilege: Users are granted only the minimum permissions needed for their role
Role-Based Access Control: Permissions are assigned based on job functions rather than individuals
Separation of Duties: Different teams have different responsibilities and access levels
Audit Trail: All actions are logged and auditable through the auditor role
Team-Based Management: Permissions are managed through teams for easier administration
